With `BOOPING_BIN` pointing at a command that exits 1, the hook absorbs the failure and exits 0,
so the transition completes and the plan stays advanced; the fake records the argv it was called
with, showing the override is the binary run. The hook's `warning: open-items follow-plan failed
(exit 1)` is not relayed here, since `transition` captures the stderr of a hook that
succeeds. `env` finds `booping` on the venv PATH the test runner runs under.

